T is the ﬁnal transcribed string (phrase) entered by the subject, and |T| is the length of this string. T may contain letters, numbers, punctuation, spaces, and other printable characters, but not backspaces. Thus, T does not capture the text entry process, but only the text entry result [26]. The S term is seconds, measured from the entry of the ﬁrst character to the entry of the last, which means that the entry of the ﬁrst character is never timed, thus the “−1” in the phrase length [26,27]. The “60” is seconds per minute and the “1/5” is words per character.
